WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.540
A friend shares a summer plan:

2
00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:07.430
«L'été prochain, j'irai en
France.» «J'irai» means I will go.

3
00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:10.350
But the French verb for go is «aller».

4
00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.050
Where did the A and the double L go?

5
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:14.390
Other verbs behave.

6
00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:17.760
«jouer», to play, becomes «je jouerai».

7
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.700
You can still see the whole verb inside.

8
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.440
So why does the French for I will go

9
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.040
look nothing like the verb for go?

10
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:30.380
In this mission, you'll track down
where that strange form comes from.

11
00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.700
Then you'll build future
forms chip by chip in the lab,

12
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.830
and predict before you check.

13
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:40.750
Your mission: find out why «j'irai»
looks nothing like «aller».
